{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The harmonic mean of two numbers can be calculated as twice their product divided by their sum. The harmonic mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is closest to which integer?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/1/45128da0142d048387cbdf21f522987455a11d2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 45 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 504 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 1008 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"430\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the harmonic mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times their product divided by their sum, we get the equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f0bbcd953286e54bf3644f679b8611bb55260b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\times1\\times2016}{1+2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"101\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>which is then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb1b684c11da5b678139637946b92fcd916800d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4032}{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>which is finally closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396b58055c2c1b0ce6cac97fa956fd300ff4307b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n-dragonfly\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You can also think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80f0bbcd953286e54bf3644f679b8611bb55260b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\times1\\times2016}{1+2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"101\" height=\"39\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55954b776192d6f5bfc2f217182d86d5d2283cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times\\frac{2016}{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" /> which it should be obvious that our number is most closest to 2 (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/966c9bd2da30d97dc51b4986eeb26dbc3aaf8fee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil\\frac{2016}{2017}\\rceil=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />), our answer here is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70432e471002b1c1f363f2d085b0f3dff8d930a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable